### 1. Anita (id=4) submits a leave request
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 4,
  "startDate": "2026-08-10",
  "endDate": "2026-08-12",
  "reason": "Wedding"
}

### 2. Check the real id this leave request got - LOOK AT THE RESPONSE, note "id"
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests?employeeId=4

### 3. Jane (id=2, Anita's REAL manager) approves it - replace {id} in URL with the real id from step 2
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests/3/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approverId": 2,
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}

### 4. Confirm it's now APPROVED
GET http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests?employeeId=4

### 5. NEGATIVE TEST: Raj (id=3, NOT Anita's manager) submits leave, Vikram tries to approve - should fail
POST http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "employeeId": 3,
  "startDate": "2026-10-01",
  "endDate": "2026-10-02",
  "reason": "Test"
}

### 6. Check the real id from step 5's response, then Vikram (id=5, not Raj's manager) tries to approve - replace {id}
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/leave-requests/4/decision
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "approverId": 5,
  "decision": "APPROVED"
}